# SHA-256 of every vendored PDFium archive, for one pinned release.
#
# Tag: chromium/8009 (PDFium 153.0.8009), published 2026-08-17.
#
# These are the digests GitHub records for the release assets themselves, read
# from the releases API, not hashes of a copy someone happened to download. A
# fetch that does not match one of these is refused: the binary ends up inside
# every yPDF build, so "it downloaded, probably fine" is not good enough.
#
# To move to a newer PDFium, change TAG in both fetch scripts and replace this
# whole file:
#
#   curl -sS https://api.github.com/repos/bblanchon/pdfium-binaries/releases/tags/chromium%2F<build> \
#     | jq -r '.assets[] | select(.name|endswith(".tgz")) | "\(.digest|sub("sha256:";""))  \(.name)"'
#
# Non-V8 builds only. yPDF detects JavaScript in a document (spec §20, §26) and
# must never be able to execute it.

c78a8cd51b48abafcb266d868e401afefda1d189aa01ebbe743dc1d144e06031  pdfium-win-x64.tgz
be513e8021a5bf8eb2116e00d78c3bacb82c5a02b3785156ae14fe5e33084385  pdfium-linux-x64.tgz
ed70360807d9e6bc4ae2b0469b576177ee9e680e73ad8216230bf8c9a6719b9c  pdfium-linux-arm64.tgz
e0afb6905e97438a9159aaa5b6c4fe188d97a7e3be05dc4782422c3ca7e1ce1a  pdfium-mac-x64.tgz
